`@wexample/js-pseudocode` turns a YAML description of code into JavaScript source: a root `items:` list whose entries are typed `constant`, `function` or `class` comes back as declarations, class bodies and JSDoc blocks built from the declared descriptions, parameters and return types, with method bodies left as `// TODO: Implement function body`. The whole public surface is one class exported from {{ path("src/index.ts") }} — `new CodeGenerator().generate(yamlText)` takes the YAML as a string and returns the code as a string, with no file access and no CLI. It is for tool authors who keep a language-neutral description of an API and need the JavaScript rendering of it, alongside the sibling generators of the Wexample suite that render the same descriptions in other languages.
